%N A399730 Number of labeled Eulerian point-determining (mating) graphs on n vertices.
%C A399730 A point-determining (mating) graph is a graph in which distinct vertices have distinct open neighborhoods. Here Eulerian means that every vertex has even degree.
%C A399730 For the general enumeration theory of point-determining graphs, see Gessel and Li.
%H A399730 I. M. Gessel and J. Li, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/0705.0042">Enumeration of Point-Determining Graphs</a>, arXiv:0705.0042 [math.CO], 2007-2009.
%F A399730 a(n) = n! * Sum_{lambda partition of n} (-1)^(n-k) E(lambda)/z_lambda, where k is the number of parts of lambda, z_lambda = Product_{j>=1} j^m_j*m_j!, and m_j is the multiplicity of j in lambda. Here E(lambda) = 2^(binomial(k,2)) if all parts of lambda are even, and E(lambda) = 2^(binomial(k-1,2)) otherwise.
%F A399730 E.g.f.: 1/2 + B(x) + B(-x^2)/2 - B(sqrt(1-x^2)-1), where B(x) is the e.g.f. of A007833. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 16 2026
%F A399730 a(n) = A007833(n) for odd n. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 15 2026
%e A399730 a(4) = 4: the four labeled Eulerian point-determining graphs on 4 vertices are the four labeled 3-cycles with one isolated vertex.
%Y A399730 Cf. A006024 (labeled point-determining graphs), A007833.
%K A399730 nonn,new
